[{"short_id":"cwmxea","created_at":"2026-11-08T11:12:00.379-06:00","title":"Playing with the STM32MP2","url":"https://serd.es///2026/11/08/playing-with-stm32mp2.html","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"fanf","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/cwmxea","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/cwmxea/playing_with_stm32mp2"},{"short_id":"umsitb","created_at":"2026-11-08T11:07:51.827-06:00","title":"What can I realistically do with local AI on a Mac mini M5 Pro (48GB)?","url":"","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eI just got a Mac mini with an M5 Pro (base CPU config) and 48GB of unified memory. I want to run as much AI locally as makes sense, but it's hard to separate what actually works day to day from benchmark hype.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I'd like to do:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCoding: autocomplete and agentic workflows with local models\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImage generation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAnything else genuinely useful: transcription, RAG over my notes, etc.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuestions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich models and quantizations fit comfortably in 48GB and are actually usable, not just \"it runs\"?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich runtime and tools: MLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, ComfyUI, something else?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhat's your setup, and what did you give up on and go back to cloud APIs for?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReal tokens/sec numbers and \"this was a waste of time\" stories are especially welcome.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I just got a Mac mini with an M5 Pro (base CPU config) and 48GB of unified memory. I want to run as much AI locally as makes sense, but it's hard to separate what actually works day to day from benchmark hype.\r\n\r\nWhat I'd like to do:\r\n\r\n- Coding: autocomplete and agentic workflows with local models\r\n- Image generation\r\n- Anything else genuinely useful: transcription, RAG over my notes, etc.\r\n\r\nQuestions:\r\n\r\n1. Which models and quantizations fit comfortably in 48GB and are actually usable, not just \"it runs\"?\r\n2. Which runtime and tools: MLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, ComfyUI, something else?\r\n3. What's your setup, and what did you give up on and go back to cloud APIs for?\r\n\r\nReal tokens/sec numbers and \"this was a waste of time\" stories are especially welcome.","submitter_user":"napolux","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ai","ask","mac"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb/what_can_i_realistically_do_with_local_ai"},{"short_id":"urg4yu","created_at":"2026-11-08T10:58:03.605-06:00","title":"Unattended reboots with encrypted disks","url":"https://jmmv.dev/2026/11/zkeys-intro.html","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jmmv","user_is_author":true,"tags":["freebsd","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/urg4yu","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/urg4yu/unattended_reboots_with_encrypted_disks"},{"short_id":"jbdtim","created_at":"2026-11-08T10:36:17.777-06:00","title":"Who wants to crowdsource LLM scans of articles submitted to Lobste.rs?","url":"","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":5,"description":"\u003cp\u003eLike many of us who value the human side of the web, I am looking for ways to keep slop at bay. It seems like LLM detection technology works reasonably well nowadays, with Pangram as the main provider. It is expensive, though!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssuming pangram scans are trustworthy, and it seems they are, we could create a centralized index of pangram scans of articles. I have already set up a \u003ca href=\"https://llm-scanner.ochagavia.nl/dashboard\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eprototype\u003c/a\u003e where I publish results of my own pangram scans. I could create more users, each tied to its own API key, so others can contribute with scans as well. This is way more resource efficient than everyone running their own scans.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you think?\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Like many of us who value the human side of the web, I am looking for ways to keep slop at bay. It seems like LLM detection technology works reasonably well nowadays, with Pangram as the main provider. It is expensive, though!\r\n\r\nAssuming pangram scans are trustworthy, and it seems they are, we could create a centralized index of pangram scans of articles. I have already set up a [prototype](https://llm-scanner.ochagavia.nl/dashboard) where I publish results of my own pangram scans. I could create more users, each tied to its own API key, so others can contribute with scans as well. This is way more resource efficient than everyone running their own scans.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?","submitter_user":"wofo","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jbdtim","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jbdtim/who_wants_crowdsource_llm_scans_articles"},{"short_id":"smx0fn","created_at":"2026-11-08T10:30:47.059-06:00","title":"SFLC.in Statement Regarding the Takedown Requests Against Its X Account and Posts","url":"https://sflc.in/sflc-in-statement-regarding-the-takedown-requests-against-its-x-account-and-posts/","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"robalex","user_is_author":false,"tags":["law"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/smx0fn","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/smx0fn/sflc_statement_regarding_takedown"},{"short_id":"b6ebju","created_at":"2026-11-08T07:21:22.648-06:00","title":"Following breadcrumbs in code - What accidentally committed Ad-Hoc logs reveal about developer comprehension","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10664-026-10988-z","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","des